infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title REST vs gRPC: optimized for different edges
  desc Same orthogonal axis, opposite jobs — pick by the edge, not the benchmark
  compares
    - label REST + OpenAPI (public edge)
      children
        - label ~20k req/s baseline
          desc Throughput is not the public edge's constraint
        - label Curl- and browser-reachable
          desc External developers hit it directly, no proxy needed
        - label OpenAPI SDKs, low onboarding
          desc Generated clients and docs from one spec
        - label Human-readable JSON
          desc Larger on the wire, but legible in DevTools and logs
    - label gRPC (internal, high volume)
      children
        - label ~50k req/s, ~77% lower latency
          desc On small payloads vs REST in synthetic benchmarks
        - label ~10x smaller messages
          desc Protobuf binary vs JSON text
        - label Native bidirectional streaming
          desc Streaming is a first-class feature, not bolted on
        - label Not browser-reachable
          desc Browsers struggle without a translating proxy
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
